            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nBehavior in video is as expected. When `z` characters are removed, the line becomes blank. In this case its indent is computed [based on previous and next non-blank lines](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c8922aef8207137e66c80acdb9523668599ba62a/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L258-L262). In this case (assuming default `config.options.border` being `'both'`) it will be the same as both `if ...` and `}` lines. So it shows a scope of lines which have at least this indent ([as per definition](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c8922aef8207137e66c80acdb9523668599ba62a/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L8-L11)) and it happens to be the parent `for` scope.\r\n\r\nClosing as working as expected.",
