            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Thanks, sorry I did not read the documentation carefully. May I suggest that distinguish between zero length lines and lines containing only blank characters and tabs, because the former is what we really want to ignore but the latter makes sense taking into account like the video ( sometimes I want to `dai` on the not yet completed if).\r\n\r\nThese changes seems be enough\r\n```diff\r\nmini.indentscope git:(main) ✗ git --no-pager diff HEAD                                                                  0 [01:40:40]\r\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/indentscope.lua b/lua/mini/indentscope.lua\r\nindex 17ab936..521a83f 100644\r\n--- a/lua/mini/indentscope.lua\r\n+++ b/lua/mini/indentscope.lua\r\n@@ -728,6 +728,9 @@ end\r\n -- - Depends on `MiniIndentscope.config.options.border` in such way so as to\r\n --   ignore blank lines before line not recognized as border.\r\n H.get_line_indent = function(line, opts)\r\n+  if vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, line - 1, line, false)[1] ~= \"\" then\r\n+    return vim.fn.indent(line)\r\n+  end\r\n   local prev_nonblank = vim.fn.prevnonblank(line)\r\n   local res = vim.fn.indent(prev_nonblank)\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2024-11-29T17:26:57Z",
