        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> May I suggest that distinguish between zero length lines and lines containing only blank characters and tabs, because the former is what we really want to ignore but the latter makes sense taking into account like the video ( sometimes I want to `dai` on the not yet completed if).\r\n\r\nI don't think that is a good idea. Mostly because of the nature of the indent itself: it is a whitespace before the \"main part\" of the line. With blank lines any separation might result in indent and main part.\r\n\r\nPlus, blank lines are not ignored: their indent is computed based on the surroundings.\r\n\r\nSo although I can understand the issue of not being able to `dai` in this case, I don't this this is going to change.",
