            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > With blank lines any separation might result in indent and main part.\r\n> \r\n> I don't understand that, could you give me an example?\r\n\r\nThe line `\\t\\t` can (in theory) be considered as\r\n- `''` indent and `'\\t\\t'` main part.\r\n- `'\\t'` indent and `'\\t'` main part.\r\n- `'\\t\\t'` indent and `''` main part.\r\n\r\nIf define \"main part\" as \"any non-whitespace charater\", then there is none in blank lines. So fall back to neighbor lines.",
